{{also|Quine}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Decapitalization of {{m|en|Quine}}.
{{named-after|en|occ=philosopher and logician|Willard Van Orman Quine|wplink==}}.
Senses related to self-reference are {{coin|en|Douglas Hofstadter|in=1979|nocap=1}} in his book ''{{w|Gödel, Escher, Bach}}'' (referencing the {{w|lang=en|Quine's paradox|paradox named after him}}), while the verb sense of “to deny the importance or significance of something” was independently {{coin|en|Daniel Dennett|nocap=1}} in ''{{w|The Philosophical Lexicon}}''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/kwaɪn/}}
